## Quick Reference Matrix

| Module | Admin Access | Team Lead Access | STL Access | Access-Based User |
|--------|-------------|------------------|------------|-------------------|
| Resource | Full CRUD, all categories | CRUD within category | View within category | Permission-based |
| Callout | Full CRUD, all categories | CRUD within category | View within category | Permission-based |
| Destination Matrix | View all, share to utilities | View team/category only | View team/category only | Permission-based |
| Roster | Full CRUD, all categories | CRUD within category | View within category | Permission-based |
| Form Generator | Full CRUD, all forms | CRUD within category | View within category | Submit & view own |
| User Access Mgmt | Full user management | View team users | View team users | View/edit own profile |

## Integration with Existing Rules

This business rules documentation **complements** the existing workspace rules:

- **Existing rules** define **how** to implement (technical patterns)
- **Business rules** define **what** to implement (business logic and constraints)

Both must be followed for correct implementation.

## Maintenance

- **When adding new features**: Update relevant module/role documentation
- **When changing business logic**: Update rules before implementing
- **During code reviews**: Verify implementation matches documented rules
- **For onboarding**: Start with `docs/business-rules/README.md`

## Notes

- All rule files are templates ready to be filled with specific business logic
- Rules should be kept up-to-date with actual implementation
- Rules are version-controlled alongside code
- Rules serve as single source of truth for business requirements